claim.claim-text:
receiving audio data (7) comprising a plurality of channels and its relevant metadata, wherein the relevant metadata includes metadata indicating a loudness of the audio data;
downmixing the audio data (7) comprising the plurality of channels into a downmixed audio signal;
determining gain values (4) based on the loudness of the audio data;
determining whether the gain values (4) are sufficient for clipping protection of the downmixed audio signal; wherein the gain values (4) are sufficient for clipping protection, if application of the gain values (4) prevents an amplitude of the downmixed audio signal from exceeding a maximum representable value;
in response to determining that the gain values (4) are sufficient for clipping protection, applying the gain values (4) to the downmixed audio signal,
in case the gain values (4) are not sufficient for clipping protection, replacing the gain values (4) with new gain values (9) sufficient for clipping protection, such that application of the new gain values (9) prevents the amplitude of the downmixed audio signal from exceeding the maximum representable value; and applying the new gain values (9) to the downmixed audio signal.

